{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/241521-abmortals","id":241521,"title":"Abmortals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-26T11:36:32-07:00","id":241521,"title":"Abmortals","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> It's been a while since I was here, but I'm gearing up for a 3 time-zone (count 'em) one shot over skype or the like. (London, Ca, and Australia. This is how I roll)<br /> <br /> So, I've got a nice (I think) framing device for a &quot;opening sting&quot; mission to get them into it, and then I'm going to frame it at a Carnivale style event on Coney Island (or, more accurately, my interpretation of Coney Island).<br /> <br /> I'm struggling with a one-shot style problem for the 3 Sin Eaters to deal with, and was wondering if an Abmortal wouldn't be a good idea. But thing is, I'm dry on ideas of what they're like.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have examples of Abmortals that worked for them?<br /> <br /> In the meanwhile, here's hoping for Geist v2...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3192-baileyborough","name":"baileyborough","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T13:38:36-07:00","id":241670,"title":"","content":"I've got an Abmortal I used once. I don't know if it'd be any good for you, though. The main problem with using a character like that is that there's no built in reason for the PCs to care. They could hear about strange deaths, or even sad ghosts, and just go on eating falafel and playing rigged games.<br /> <br /> My Abmortal was a man named Clarence Daniels. Young shell shocked soldier who's dad gave him one of those overly strict training regimes even before he was a soldier, but couldn't hack it when it came to the real thing, that kind of thing. He started killing people with supernatural talents and using a ritual he learned to eat their ghosts and get their numina. The PCs stumbled across the corpse of his last victim, and saw the way the sigil drawn in her blood was trapping her, and slowly tearing away at her corpus. Also it made her a ghost even if she shouldn't have been. Daniels had done this to a few people before, and they were all part of a supernatural &quot;book club&quot;. Think the Ordo Lebes from Dresden Files. A bunch of people with small talents hanging out and talking about how they could push stuff with their mind and trying to be a support group.<br /> <br /> An alternate and more refined version that I haven't gotten around to using is a different version of the same concept of a ghost eater. Woman, mid twenties, lesbian, from a religious household. Her parents were strict and abusive to the point of cartoonish, and she stopped being attracted to girls for a while, as well as stopped using her mind control powers. They stopped beating her and calling her a witch. Then when she was in college she snapped, and ended up killing someone. She was jealous of the book club--who still had their powers and were accepted by each other for them--while she was repressed and self-loathing. So she killed them, and took their powers. Repression was a theme of that story, with supernatural powers basically being a big gay metaphor.<br /> <br /> I also had a tie in to my larger story, where Clarence's 'spell' was found in his Haunt, and his notes talked about a &quot;Man in White&quot; and a &quot;Man in Black&quot; that gave him the ritual. That guy was an Abmortal who died in a car accident and was revived by the EMTs. He ended up delving into the supernatural and he forcibly bound a Geist to him (The Man in Black). He was going to be going around making Abmortals and trying to find an apprentice. One of the PCs was going to be it (he killed her with his car, was dating her mother). <hr /> <hr />For <i>you</i>, though? I'd suggest something that uses the carnival itself. Maybe someone attacking it like a terrorist, or maybe someone who steals a friend of the group for something heinous, and they have until the carnival is over to figure it out and put a stop to it. Make time matter. The PCs have to hurry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T13:24:21-07:00","id":243360,"title":"","content":"Some quick thoughts on your suggestion:<br /> <br /> For Abmortal #1 (the soldier) - to make him relevant, maybe think about what he's doing with his immortality. Perhaps he's learned of Sin-Eaters and has decided to kill anyone who learns of his secret. Or perhaps what happened to the ghost isn't so obvious and she's easily freed - only to trigger a bad reaction in Daniels and send him hunting after the ghost that was sent on to her afterlife too quickly.<br /> <br /> For the second: Well, she's already hunting people with powers. Maybe she comes after the group by accident with her supercharged powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}